    "turn_text": "But there's nobody yet announced for Minister of Defense. So it's very hard to have that conversation without it. It's one of the big outcomes of it. I do think, and you and I talked about this in San Francisco, and I think this is, I think, an opportunity, not just with China, but for the United States. And we're sitting here doing this meeting while COP 28 is happening. And Dubai. Climate. AI. And you'd have to say global pandemics, given that the pneumonia that just looks like it broke out in China, not looks like it did. It did, yeah. And so when you look at all of those, and then you look at the architecture that set up post World War II, I think these new challenges give us an opportunity to modernize an initiated system to manage both current and future threats. that we have self-interest. But it requires a level of trust and a level of transparency that if you want to be a global leader, you're going to have to sign on to. And you have an opportunity, you want to be part of the global order that you are rules-based system that you think you had some role in playing. OK, let's go. And I think that's what the president laid down. When you really kind of blow through all the smoke, whether it was on climate, whether it was on AI, drugs in a sense of subgroups like gangs and drug dealers dealing with fentanyl and you deal with kind of pandemics or future pandemics. calling on China to be a global leader with global responsibilities. You can't allow another kind of almost potential public health crisis and don't become fully transparent with the international community. That's just not a global leader. The reality is there was no level of cooperation from the Chinese government",
